From: 梦龙 <chen.menglong@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: declare ssdk_switch_set_standby_status outside the DSA guard

ssdk_switch_set_standby_status() is defined unconditionally in
src/init/ssdk_plat.c: the IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_DSA) in that function
guards only the DSA notification inside its body. Its declaration in
include/init/ssdk_plat.h nevertheless sits inside the CONFIG_NET_DSA
block that holds the genuinely DSA-only ssdk_switch_enable_dsa().

src/hsl/mht/mht_port_ctrl.c calls it unconditionally, so with
CONFIG_NET_DSA disabled the call compiles without a prototype and is an
implicit declaration, which GCC 15 (C23) rejects. Move the declaration
out of the guard, next to ssdk_netdev_switch_init(), so that it is
visible wherever the definition is compiled.

---
# Not from the pinned fork. Delete this patch once the pinned revision
# declares ssdk_switch_set_standby_status outside its CONFIG_NET_DSA guard.

--- a/include/init/ssdk_plat.h
+++ b/include/init/ssdk_plat.h
@@ -506,5 +506,5 @@
 sw_error_t ssdk_netdev_switch_init(struct net_device *dev);
+void ssdk_switch_set_standby_status(a_uint32_t dev_id, bool enable);
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_DSA)
-void ssdk_switch_set_standby_status(a_uint32_t dev_id, bool enable);
 a_bool_t ssdk_switch_enable_dsa(a_uint32_t dev_id);
 #endif
 #endif
